-- title:
--   Places over a supersingular node counted by crossing-model branches
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a nonzero level $N$, a perfect, algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $q$ with a ring map $red : A \to k$, modular polynomial data for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence, integrality of the two degeneracy maps $\bar\alpha,\bar\beta$ at level $N,q$, a place specialisation $P$ for these data and a prolongation tuple $R$ over $P$; assume $q \nmid N$ and that $R$ satisfies `OrderLawFixed`. Let $K \subset \overline{\mathbb Q}$ be a finite extension of $\mathbb Q$ and $w$ a place of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ k\ N$ lying in $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\ q\ N\ k$, so $w$ is rational, both $j$ and $j_N$ are $w$-integral, and the value of $j$ at $w$ is supersingular in characteristic $q$. Write $B = R.\mathrm{nodeIntegersOver}\ K\ w$ for the ring of elements of the level-$Nq$ function field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(Nq)$ integral for both prolongations $R_1, R_2$, integral at every place $V$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(Nq)$ with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\ V = w$, and with Laurent expansion in $\mathrm{NodeLocalized.fieldOver}(Nq)\ K$; let $\mathcal O = \mathrm{NodeLocalized.coeffSubring}\ A\ K = A \cap K$, with $\mathrm{nodeConst}$ the inclusion of $\mathcal O$ into $B$ as constants. The hypotheses on $B$ are: node coordinates $c = (x,y)$ (so the first residue of $x$ vanishes and the Frobenius-twisted second residue of $x$ has order $1$, and symmetrically for $y$); a nonzero $\varpi \in \mathcal O$ with $B$ local noetherian and maximal ideal $(\mathrm{nodeConst}\,\varpi, x, y)$; every $g \in B$ is congruent to some constant modulo non-units ($g - \mathrm{nodeConst}\,o$ a non-unit for some $o$); the value integrality law at $w$ (values at places over $w$ of node integers lie in $A$); every prime strictly below a non-maximal prime of $B$ is $\bot$; and every element of $\mathrm{NodeLocalized.fieldOver}(Nq)\ K$ is a quotient of elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator. Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation domain with irreducible $\pi$, $E \ge 1$, and $\iota$ a ring isomorphism from the $\mathfrak m_B$-adic completion of $B$ onto $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\ W\ (\pi^E) = W[[U,V]]/(UV - \pi^E)$ sending $\mathrm{nodeConst}\,\varpi$ to $\mathrm{const}\,\pi$ and $x$ to $U$ times a unit $\alpha_U$; assume $\mathcal O$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal $(\varpi)$ and $\tau$ an isomorphism of its completion with $W$ sending $\varpi$ to $\pi$ and compatible with $\iota$ on constants; assume further the two order-reading clauses: for $g \in B$ and $n \in \mathbb N$, if the first residue of $g$ is nonzero of $w$-order $n$ then $\iota(g) - \gamma V^n \in (\mathrm{const}\,\pi, U)$ for some unit $\gamma$, and symmetrically with the second residue, the Frobenius-twisted place, $U^n$ and $(\mathrm{const}\,\pi, V)$. Finally let $\mathfrak q$ be a nonzero prime of $B$ containing no nonzero constant, and let $S$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}(Nq)$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ consisting exactly of those $V$ with $P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\ V = w$ whose kernel of evaluation on $B$ is precisely $\mathfrak q$. The conclusion is that the cardinality of $S$, read in $\mathbb N_\infty$, equals the sum over those points $Q$ of the prime spectrum of $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi^E)$ that are minimal primes of the ideal generated by the image of $\mathfrak q$ under $\iota$ composed with the completion map and satisfy $\mathrm{const}\,\pi \notin Q$, of the $W$-rank of the quotient of the crossing model by $Q$.
--
--   This is the place–model dictionary at a supersingular node of $X_0(Nq)$ in its kernel-of-evaluation form: the places of the level-$Nq$ function field above a fixed supersingular place $w$ whose evaluation kernel on the ring of node integers is a given nonzero prime $\mathfrak q$ are counted exactly by the total $W$-rank of the horizontal branches of the crossing model $W[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi^E)$ through the corresponding ideal. It is used to extract, from the crossing-model description, a place over $w$ together with the prescribed values and orders of the node coordinates.
